> Why naked?  I've never heard that one before.

It's a common fallacy. Some people think that the priest only looks at you
apparent AC and won't sell you protection if it's 1 or less; but in fact
priests see your intrinsic AC (as if you were naked) no matter what
you're wearing, and sell you protection based on that. Taking off armor
is unnecessary, and in a cross-aligned temple it's foolish.

You get up to 3 (I think) points on the first donation, after that 1 point
per donation until you're at intrinsic 1, after that it's a chance of 
1 in (10 - current intrinsic AC) for another point, with a limit of
intrinsic -10.

   Raisse, killed by a priestess of Anhur

